Project Planning & Presentation 

Project Implementation Plan (Module Breakdown):
	1. Requirements & Scope Finalization (Week 1):
		* Collect and confirm CO₂ AT3 capstone requirements
		* Define user roles, functional requirements, constraints, and success criteria
	2. Existing System Analysis (Week 2):
		* Study current/related solutions
		* Identify gaps and define improvement points
		* Decide what features the proposed system will include
	3. System Design & Architecture (Week 3–4):
		* Finalize system architecture and data flow
		* Create UML diagrams: Use Case, Class, and Sequence diagrams
		* Define database schema and APIs/endpoints
	4. Technology Stack Setup (Week 3–4):
		* Initialize repository and project structure
		* Configure Java IDE (Eclipse/IntelliJ), build setup, and dependencies
		* Prepare MySQL database and JDBC connectivity
	5. Module Development (Week 5–7):
		* Implement modules for data capture/input, validation, and storage
		* Develop processing/calculation logic
		* Implement module-wise unit testing and bug fixes
	6. Integration & UI Implementation (Week 8):
		* Integrate backend modules end-to-end
		* Create/refine UI screens (forms, dashboards, and reports/output views)
		* Validate full workflow from input → processing → results
	7. Testing & Validation (Week 9):
		* Perform functional testing, edge-case testing, and regression testing
		* Verify database persistence, correctness of results, and usability
		* Improve performance and reliability based on test outcomes
	8. Final Documentation & Presentation Preparation (Week 10):
		* Prepare final report, diagrams, and documentation
		* Create presentation slides and demo workflow
		* Final review and submission

Gantt Chart (Expected Timeline):

	* Week 1: Requirements & Scope Finalization
	* Week 2: Existing System Analysis
	* Week 3–4: System Design + Technology Stack Setup
	* Week 5–7: Module Development
	* Week 8: Integration & UI Implementation
	* Week 9: Testing & Validation
	* Week 10: Documentation + Final Demo

Technology Stack:

	* Java (main application)
	* IDE: Eclipse/IntelliJ
	* JDBC (database connectivity)
	* SQL / MySQL (data storage)
	* Git/GitHub (version control)
	* HTML/CSS/Bootstrap (if web UI is used)
	* UML tools (optional)

Expected Timeline & Milestones:

	* End of Week 2: Requirements + analysis complete
	* End of Week 4: System design + database + modules ready for coding
	* End of Week 7: Core functionality completed
	* End of Week 9: System tested and validated
	* End of Week 10: Final demo + report submission

Initial Prototype (if available):

	* Basic input flow for CO₂-related data
	* Core processing/calculation and validation logic
	* Database persistence for storing inputs and generated outputs
	* Preliminary UI screens for data entry and viewing results

Future Work:

	* Add advanced analytics (trend graphs, predictions/insights)
	* Enhance dashboards and reporting for better user experience
	* Add role-based access (Admin/User/Viewer)
	* Provide export features (PDF/CSV)
	* If applicable, integrate external sensors/APIs in later versions

Response to Review Committee Questions (Brief):

	* How will you measure success?
By verifying accurate processing results, successful database storage, correct UI workflow, and successful end-to-end demo after testing.

	* What risk do you foresee?
Data accuracy issues, integration delays, and UI responsiveness—mitigated through frequent testing, modular development, and early integration.

	* Why this architecture?
It ensures modularity, easier testing, maintainability, and allows future upgrades without major redesign.
